course: dictionary
lesson: 15147
title: Scholarly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scholarly describes someone who studies a lot and knows a great deal about a subject. It can also describe serious, careful writing. Look at the words around it for clues. «Maya read a scholarly article before she wrote her project.» The article was written by experts, so it must be careful and trustworthy.
explain: Scholarly can also describe a person or a way of behaving. «The scholarly librarian had read every book on the shelves.» A librarian who has read every book is a learned person who loves study, so scholarly means knowing a lot and loving learning.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Maya read a serious, careful article written by experts» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood the word. If it does not fit, read on and look for more clues.
fact: Scholarly is an adjective: scholarly, more scholarly, most scholarly.
fact: «Scholarly» means studying a lot and knowing a great deal about a subject.
fact: A «scholarly article» is serious writing by experts, with facts checked and sources given.
fact: A «scholarly man» might be a professor, a librarian or a wise old person surrounded by books.
fact: For a school project, a scholarly source is usually more trustworthy than a random web page.
exercise: «The scholarly article was written by experts and listed all its sources.» What does scholarly mean here? | *Careful, serious writing by experts | Written in a hurry by a child | Silly and full of jokes | Very short and quick
exercise: For a school project, which source is more trustworthy? | A post with no sources | A random web page with no name | A funny comic | *A scholarly journal written by experts
exercise: Which word means knowing a great deal from study? | silly | scruffy | sleepy | *scholarly
test: «The old professor, scholarly and quiet, read his books every night.» What does scholarly describe? | His new car | His fast running | *His studying and learning | His loud singing
test: Ella says scholarly means messy. Why is she wrong? | Scholarly means messy and loud | Scholarly means fast | Scholarly means funny | *Scholarly means studying a lot and knowing a great deal
exam: Which sentence uses scholarly correctly? | We had scholarly sandwiches for lunch | The scholarly dog barked at the postman | *The librarian, a scholarly woman, knew every book on the shelves | The scholarly sun was hot all day
